  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/pseudomugil-signifer",
      "html": "<ul><li>Schooling rainbowfish, yellowish orange with white accents on the fins and blue eyes.</li><li>Colours are best when breeding.</li><li>Size: 1.5 - 2.5 inches (about 4 - 6 cm).</li><li>Kept at around 22-25°C (72-77°F) and pH of roughly 6.5-7.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/pseudomugil-signifer",
      "html": "<p>Pseudomugil species can hybridize, so you may want to keep them with other types of small rainbowfish or tetras and rasboras of similar size. They also do well with Neocaridina and Caridina shrimps.</p>"
    }
